Subject: clk: qcom: camcc-sc8280xp: mark the camnoc_axi, slow_ahb and fast_ahb RCGs shared

Measured with the camera power domain pinned on and one CAMSS run: after the
camera has used its clocks, camcc_camnoc_axi_clk_src stays pointed at
camcc_pll0_out_even with that PLL off (rate 150 MHz, enabled 0), where it
sits on the always-on XO before any use. That is the one hardware difference
between a clean collapse of titan_top_gdsc and the dirty one that leaves
CFG_GDSCR without bit 19 and freezes the next power-up FSM: CAMNOC cannot
complete the GDSC handshake without a live clock.

clk_rcg2_shared_ops parks the RCG on its safe source (XO) at disable and at
probe; plain clk_rcg2_ops has no disable callback and keeps the last set_rate
source. 21 of the driver's 43 RCGs are already shared, but camnoc_axi,
slow_ahb (the source of cpas_ahb) and fast_ahb are not. x1e80100 marks
exactly these three shared while leaving cci, cphy and csiXphytimer plain,
and sm8150/sc8180x mark all RCGs shared; this follows x1e80100.

This is the root-cause fix for the gaokun3 camera power-domain defect, where
every second capture failed after the domain had been used once. Written for
upstream together with the GDSC wait values in the previous patch.
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sc8280xp.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sc8280xp.c
index e4ec7e3..5ba6e54 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sc8280xp.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sc8280xp.c
@@ -667,7 +667,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 camcc_camnoc_axi_clk_src = {
 		.name = "camcc_camnoc_axi_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = camcc_parent_data_2,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(camcc_parent_data_2),
-		.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_ops,
 	},
 };
 
@@ -835,7 +835,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 camcc_fast_ahb_clk_src = {
 		.name = "camcc_fast_ahb_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = camcc_parent_data_0,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(camcc_parent_data_0),
-		.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_ops,
 	},
 };
 
@@ -1370,7 +1370,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 camcc_slow_ahb_clk_src = {
 		.name = "camcc_slow_ahb_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = camcc_parent_data_0,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(camcc_parent_data_0),
-		.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_ops,
 	},
 };
 
